Chapter: QemuVirtBoard
  cites Foreword chapter Board

 Board constants for QEMU -M virt (AArch64 and RISC-V).
 These are the memory-mapped peripheral addresses from the
 QEMU virt machine model. Used by the codegen plugs for
 boot stubs and UART output.

 The UART helpers reach the bus, so every one of them declares
 [Device.Mmio]. The row is what makes the access visible to the effect
 system, to the capability manifest, and to the boot grant. A driver
 that writes hardware while typed pure is a driver the machine cannot
 see. The character decoding in the loops touches no register, so it
 stays in a pure let ahead of the act block.

Section: QEMU AArch64 Virt

  qemu-a64-pl011-base : Integer = #09000000
  qemu-a64-pl011-dr : Integer = #09000000
  qemu-a64-pl011-fr : Integer = #09000018
  qemu-a64-gic-dist : Integer = #08000000
  qemu-a64-gic-cpu : Integer = #08010000
  qemu-a64-ram-base : Integer = #40000000
  qemu-a64-flash-base : Integer = #00000000

Section: QEMU RISC-V Virt

  qemu-rv-uart-base : Integer = #10000000
  qemu-rv-uart-thr : Integer = #10000000
  qemu-rv-uart-lsr : Integer = #10000005
  qemu-rv-clint-base : Integer = #02000000
  qemu-rv-plic-base : Integer = #0C000000
  qemu-rv-ram-base : Integer = #80000000

Section: UART Helpers

  qemu-a64-uart-putc : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-a64-uart-putc (c) = mmio-write-8 qemu-a64-pl011-dr c

  qemu-a64-uart-puts : Text -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-a64-uart-puts (s) = qemu-a64-uart-puts-loop s 0 (text-length s)

  qemu-a64-uart-puts-loop : Text, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-a64-uart-puts-loop (s) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then 0
   else let c = char-code (char-at s i)
   in act
    w <- (qemu-a64-uart-putc c)
    qemu-a64-uart-puts-loop s (i + 1) len
   end

  qemu-rv-uart-putc : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-rv-uart-putc (c) = mmio-write-8 qemu-rv-uart-thr c

  qemu-rv-uart-puts : Text -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-rv-uart-puts (s) = qemu-rv-uart-puts-loop s 0 (text-length s)

  qemu-rv-uart-puts-loop : Text, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  qemu-rv-uart-puts-loop (s) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then 0
   else let c = char-code (char-at s i)
   in act
    w <- (qemu-rv-uart-putc c)
    qemu-rv-uart-puts-loop s (i + 1) len
   end

